// REJECTS: Unexpected token '~filter'
//
// A relational class mapping's modifiers are ordered:
//     ~filter? ~distinct? ~groupBy? ~primaryKey? ~mainTable?
// ~mainTable is LAST. This writes it first, which is where every reader would put it --
// naming the table you are mapping before filtering it.
//
// The stress corpus and the positive fixtures only ever write ~mainTable alongside
// ~primaryKey, so the constraint is invisible to them: a rewrite can accept the modifiers
// in any order and pass every fixture that exists. Swapping these two lines makes it parse.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::MainTableFirst
(
   fixture::neg::Person: Relational
   {
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db]T
      ~filter [fixture::neg::Db] ActiveFilter
      id: [fixture::neg::Db]T.ID
   }
)
